    "scale_note": "Cells retain true scale: 0.03 build units per micrometre. The layout is a selected comparison, not a smear, blood differential or volume fraction. Eight leukocyte examples, three whole erythrocytes, a seven-cell rouleau, one erythrocyte section and four resting platelets are illustrative. T/B receptor symbols are greatly enlarged functional cues and cannot identify T/B cells on Wright stain. Granules are enlarged, reduced representative samples. The Clot view shows two activated platelets and ten sampled connected fibrin paths; these counts and fibre thickness are schematic. Antibody secretion requires activated B-lineage plasmablast/plasma-cell differentiation, which is not modeled.",
    "summary": "Compare blood-cell shape at a shared physical scale. Smear comparison hides the enlarged T/B receptor symbols; Receptor function explains their distinct recognition roles. Follow red-cell shape, granulocyte nuclei and granules, resting lymphocyte morphology and monocyte structure, then the separate static Clot and optional Plasma context views. Cell counts and arrangement are illustrative."
